From 1fb984aa3390f921c4cc9702b582f011e547b722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosetta <cole@phosphor.co>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:46:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(multiplayer): port identity and presence onto
 current upstream

- Re-express the accepted multiplayer identity, authorship, presence, member,
  Connect, SDK, CLI, and UI intents against current upstream architecture.
- Preserve current queue transactions, SQLite batching, update guidance,
  protocol lineage, and generated-template ownership while moving identity
  schema history to the additive 0107 migration.
- Derive PrincipalKeys only from server-authenticated provider identity; client
  claims may decorate an authenticated socket presentation but cannot select
  HTTP/socket principals or authored identity.
- Verify the port through package typechecks and focused DB, server, app, SDK,
  CLI, Connect, tunnel, host-daemon, and thread-view behavior suites.

